Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-02-28T09:11:40Z","updated_at":"2026-08-29T00:17:21Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 3.6 (mono)\n- Not reproducible in 3.5.3 (mono)\n\n### System information\n\nAndroid 14, Google Chrome, GLES2. (Confirmed on other devices and other browsers)\n\n### Issue description\n\nLineEdit and TextEdit seem to be broken for mobile web in version 3.6.\nAfter migrating my project from 3.5.3 to 3.6, it stopped working. So it looks to be a regression. On 3.6, I am able to open the keyboard, and type characters, but the characters do not show up in the LineEdit.\n\nHow it looks in 3.6:\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2f48e0ae-dad9-4427-b5da-6c8f5f70262c)\n\nHow it looks in 3.5.3\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c6c0ad60-da2d-4729-8d75-134029edc3ad)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a scene with a Panel as root node\n- Place a LineEdit node in the scene\n- Save the scene and set it as main scene\n- Export the project to HTML5 *Enable \"Experimental Virtual Keyboard\"\n- Open the app on a mobile browser (For example, deploy the project on Itch.io or use a local web server to access it on a mobile browser)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[LineEdit.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19025031/LineEdit.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103387/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103387/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}